        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "These essays were also badly organized in several ways. In the first two essays after training began, the students visibly attempted to distinguish fact from opinion but did so inconsistently. They also produced fewer spelling and punctuation errors. In essays four through seven, they distinguished fact from opinion more consistently, but in their final essay, written six months after completion of instruction, they did no better than they did in their first essay. Their last essay was significantly longer than their first one, however. Their training thus had some effect on their writing during the training period, but it was inconsistent and transient.",
            "block_bbox": [
                115,
                117,
                742,
                307
            ],
            "block_id": 2,
            "block_order": 1,
            "group_id": 2,
            "global_block_id": 2,
